{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And on the seventh day, Shabbat.</b> Those of deficient faith say that the day and the night that follows it is the day of Shabbat, and their proof is that Moshe said, 'Shabbat today to YHWH,' and not the night that passed; he also said, 'tomorrow.' But they did not speak correctly, for we find: 'בערב תאכלו מצות' — 'in the evening you shall eat matzot' — 'עד יום האחד ועשרים לחדש בערב' — 'until the twenty-first day of the month, in the evening.' And it says, 'מערב עד ערב תשבתו שבתכם' — 'from evening to evening you shall observe your Shabbat.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:14.702643214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}